(3356263, 466917, 36382, '<td valign="top">This is nice the veg looks good.  There is a black spot next to the yellow pepper on the left.  I like the textures of the garlic and onion next to the smooth tomatoes and peppers.</td>', 'This is nice the veg looks good.  There is a black spot next to the yellow pepper on the left.  I like the textures of the garlic and onion next to the smooth tomatoes and peppers.', '2007-02-12 08:16:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(3356267, 466724, 43463, '<td valign="top">A very creative and good composition! But it is the expression on the model that has me wondering: "Should the magician be surprised at the magic he/she casts from their own hands or should they have a cool &amp; composed mysterious look about them as they cast their magic?" I don''t know but it is one thing that makes me pause as I look upon this photo. Heh, you know what I just realized? You almost followed an artist''s color wheel pattern! Had you positioned the yellows together to fade into the oranges then fade into the reds you would have a perfect fruit &amp; vege color wheel! O.K. tones are very good with the small exception that the sleeve &amp; hand of the foreground arm blends in a tad too well with the outstretched arm. Not sure how to correct it to make them a little more distinct in tones - a tiny bit of dodging mayhap??? The colors of the fruits and vegetables really pop off the page. The striped wallpaper as the backdrop is a tad distracting to the main composition as a whole. But in an odd way it can help add to the illusion of that of a magician standing on a ''curtained'' stage performing his/her magic tricks.</td>', 'A very creative and good composition! But it is the expression on the model that has me wondering: "Should the magician be surprised at the magic he/she casts from their own hands or should they have a cool & composed mysterious look about them as they cast their magic?" I don''t know but it is one thing that makes me pause as I look upon this photo. Heh, you know what I just realized? You almost followed an artist''s color wheel pattern! Had you positioned the yellows together to fade into the oranges then fade into the reds you would have a perfect fruit & vege color wheel! O.K. tones are very good with the small exception that the sleeve & hand of the foreground arm blends in a tad too well with the outstretched arm. Not sure how to correct it to make them a little more distinct in tones - a tiny bit of dodging mayhap??? The colors of the fruits and vegetables really pop off the page. The striped wallpaper as the backdrop is a tad distracting to the main composition as a whole. But in an odd way it can help add to the illusion of that of a magician standing on a ''curtained'' stage performing his/her magic tricks.', '2007-02-12 08:20:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(3356303, 465304, 15711, '<td valign="top">I like the line of the spoon but the berries just kind of come off rather flat. Maybe a selective saturation of a hint of the berry color would have helped it more for me.</td>', 'I like the line of the spoon but the berries just kind of come off rather flat. Maybe a selective saturation of a hint of the berry color would have helped it more for me.', '2007-02-12 08:35:28.000000', NULL, 1),
