(3373316, 466510, 9906, '<td valign="top">Looks like your a touch overexposed.  It also looks like your colors may be off just at ouch.  Yellow is a tricky color for the web for some reason...<br/>TC</td>', 'Looks like your a touch overexposed.  It also looks like your colors may be off just at ouch.  Yellow is a tricky color for the web for some reason...TC', '2007-02-16 17:32:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3373317, 466387, 9906, '<td valign="top">This is a bit too busy.  A closer crop of just one fruit may have worked better.  This way there is just too much going on and no where for your eye to rest...<br/>TC</td>', 'This is a bit too busy.  A closer crop of just one fruit may have worked better.  This way there is just too much going on and no where for your eye to rest...TC', '2007-02-16 17:33:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(3373319, 466883, 9906, '<td valign="top">Your dof is quite shallow which doesn''t seem to work too well here.  I can''t figure out where your point of focus is and that is confusing to the eye.<br/>TC</td>', 'Your dof is quite shallow which doesn''t seem to work too well here.  I can''t figure out where your point of focus is and that is confusing to the eye.TC', '2007-02-16 17:34:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(3373323, 467245, 9906, '<td valign="top">Damn...  too bad for that little sticker under the thumb...  Otherwise this shot is the bomb!</td>', 'Damn...  too bad for that little sticker under the thumb...  Otherwise this shot is the bomb!', '2007-02-16 17:35:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(3373330, 467425, 9906, '<td valign="top">I''m trying to figure out how this was lit and am leaning towards you having used the flash.  I''m also assumning the flash is on the left side of your camera.  When doing a studio shot like this I would recommend never using your flash.  Turn the dang thing off.  Put the camera on a tripod or other solid object and use the timer to take the picture.  Let the camera use a long exposure.  Then you can play around with moving the lights around to get cool effects.<br/>TC</td>', 'I''m trying to figure out how this was lit and am leaning towards you having used the flash.  I''m also assumning the flash is on the left side of your camera.  When doing a studio shot like this I would recommend never using your flash.  Turn the dang thing off.  Put the camera on a tripod or other solid object and use the timer to take the picture.  Let the camera use a long exposure.  Then you can play around with moving the lights around to get cool effects.TC', '2007-02-16 17:37:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(3373333, 467123, 9906, '<td valign="top">Wow.  I almost love this shot.  I''m finding the white bar of light to be a big distraction though.  If it was redish, goldish like the rest of the bars of light this would be a fascinating shot!<br/>Kudos<br/>TC</td>', 'Wow.  I almost love this shot.  I''m finding the white bar of light to be a big distraction though.  If it was redish, goldish like the rest of the bars of light this would be a fascinating shot!KudosTC', '2007-02-16 17:38:50.000000', NULL, 1),
