(3374765, 467413, 73230, '<td valign="top">I love this image, i think its because even though i live in the UK, i know so much about Pike Place (well at least i think i do). Pike Place features in one of our training modules for new starters to the company and shows them the importance of working as a team and motivation. It shows those whacky guys throwing the fish around (now that would be a good photograph). Anyways, well done for bringing back some funny memories, isnt that what photography is about ? Memories.</td>', 'I love this image, i think its because even though i live in the UK, i know so much about Pike Place (well at least i think i do). Pike Place features in one of our training modules for new starters to the company and shows them the importance of working as a team and motivation. It shows those whacky guys throwing the fish around (now that would be a good photograph). Anyways, well done for bringing back some funny memories, isnt that what photography is about ? Memories.', '2007-02-17 09:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3374773, 467445, 60195, '<td valign="top">Of the "still Life" shots in this challenge, I thought that this one stood out as the best.  I like the subtle lighting, and clarity/sharpness is spot-on.  I looked at this one on multiple monitors, and with a darker profile - it loses a lot of it''s "pop" (infact, they look like two completely different shots). Hopefully most voters have bright profiles!  Good luck... it''s a great image :O)</td>', 'Of the "still Life" shots in this challenge, I thought that this one stood out as the best.  I like the subtle lighting, and clarity/sharpness is spot-on.  I looked at this one on multiple monitors, and with a darker profile - it loses a lot of it''s "pop" (infact, they look like two completely different shots). Hopefully most voters have bright profiles!  Good luck... it''s a great image :O)', '2007-02-17 09:43:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3374785, 467051, 60195, '<td valign="top">Interesting crop.  This stood out for me, as it was something completely different. Looking at it on multiple monitors with different profiles... unfortunately with a standard "bright" monitor this looks very yellow, and therefore looks more like a lemon than an orange. I like the juice droplet on the peel - might have been nice if you''d dodged it a bit to make that more apparent.  Nice image :O)</td>', 'Interesting crop.  This stood out for me, as it was something completely different. Looking at it on multiple monitors with different profiles... unfortunately with a standard "bright" monitor this looks very yellow, and therefore looks more like a lemon than an orange. I like the juice droplet on the peel - might have been nice if you''d dodged it a bit to make that more apparent.  Nice image :O)', '2007-02-17 09:50:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(3374793, 466683, 60195, '<td valign="top">Nice image. Looks like you went to a lot of trouble prepping for this shot :O)  It is unfortunate that the eggplant fades into the background - to the point that "on first glance" it almost looks like someone took a giant bite out of the squash(?) behind it.</td>', 'Nice image. Looks like you went to a lot of trouble prepping for this shot :O)  It is unfortunate that the eggplant fades into the background - to the point that "on first glance" it almost looks like someone took a giant bite out of the squash(?) behind it.', '2007-02-17 09:56:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(3374802, 466584, 60195, '<td valign="top">Nice image.  This had a lot of potential, as the arrangement stands out from the standard still-life shots in this challenge. Unfortunately the overall brightness of the background &amp; the highlights on the orange wedges is extremely bright.  I even looked at this on multiple monitors, and with a darker profile - it still looks very washed out. Maybe try toning down the brightness, and adding a bit of selective sharpening on the slices (the peel looks very sharp compared to the slices).  Again... very nice setup :O)</td>', 'Nice image.  This had a lot of potential, as the arrangement stands out from the standard still-life shots in this challenge. Unfortunately the overall brightness of the background & the highlights on the orange wedges is extremely bright.  I even looked at this on multiple monitors, and with a darker profile - it still looks very washed out. Maybe try toning down the brightness, and adding a bit of selective sharpening on the slices (the peel looks very sharp compared to the slices).  Again... very nice setup :O)', '2007-02-17 10:02:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(3374817, 465558, 60195, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, &amp; setup. Nice clarity &amp; color on the strawberries. I''m not sure that the direct overhead angle helps the shot. This would be nice if you had tilted the angle a bit - I think it would have caught some of the lighting better (to add some depth) &amp; might have showed some of the woodgrain &amp; bowl texture a bit better.  As it is, it comes across as very 2-dimensional.</td>', 'I like the idea, & setup. Nice clarity & color on the strawberries. I''m not sure that the direct overhead angle helps the shot. This would be nice if you had tilted the angle a bit - I think it would have caught some of the lighting better (to add some depth) & might have showed some of the woodgrain & bowl texture a bit better.  As it is, it comes across as very 2-dimensional.', '2007-02-17 10:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3374826, 466306, 60195, '<td valign="top">Nice lighting &amp; clarity. I like the idea, setup, and angle.</td>', 'Nice lighting & clarity. I like the idea, setup, and angle.', '2007-02-17 10:12:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3374841, 467377, 60195, '<td valign="top">I love the setup on this. Great contrasting ingredients, and where did you find that bowl?!  :O)  Definitely a strong contender in this challenge. The only thing I could suggest would be to crank up the color saturation on the vegetables... that would have definitely helped to make this "pop". Good luck!</td>', 'I love the setup on this. Great contrasting ingredients, and where did you find that bowl?!  :O)  Definitely a strong contender in this challenge. The only thing I could suggest would be to crank up the color saturation on the vegetables... that would have definitely helped to make this "pop". Good luck!', '2007-02-17 10:17:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(3374849, 466368, 60195, '<td valign="top">I like the idea &amp; setup here. The "frosty" glass adds a nice touch. It would definitely help this image to play with the color &amp; saturation on the fruit. As it is, the color seems washed out, and it''s hard to tell if it''s an orange, a lemon, or a lime.  Good luck :O)</td>', 'I like the idea & setup here. The "frosty" glass adds a nice touch. It would definitely help this image to play with the color & saturation on the fruit. As it is, the color seems washed out, and it''s hard to tell if it''s an orange, a lemon, or a lime.  Good luck :O)', '2007-02-17 10:22:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(3374855, 467360, 60195, '<td valign="top">Nice setup &amp; lightning. It''s hard to get that "juicy" appetizing look on the fruit, and you''ve done a great job!  My only suggestion would be to desat &amp; blur the blue background a bit. The sharpening artifacts show up quite a bit in the deep blue.  Good luck in the challenge!</td>', 'Nice setup & lightning. It''s hard to get that "juicy" appetizing look on the fruit, and you''ve done a great job!  My only suggestion would be to desat & blur the blue background a bit. The sharpening artifacts show up quite a bit in the deep blue.  Good luck in the challenge!', '2007-02-17 10:26:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3374857, 467442, 54778, '<td valign="top">very cool setup.. I like how everything looks like its meant to be..</td>', 'very cool setup.. I like how everything looks like its meant to be..', '2007-02-17 10:26:29.000000', NULL, 1),
