(3381309, 467075, 61818, '<td valign="top">This would look better if something in it were sharp, preferably the vegetables.  Lowering your aperture would allow you to increase your shutter speed and freeze the motion.  This would certainly sharpen things up.<br/> <br/>Losing the yellow tint in the air bubbles on the left side would also help.  The picture would have much more impact with just the color of the vegetables, the white of the water, and the black background.<br/> <br/>Really the big issue here is not freezing the motion.<br/> <br/>Hope that helps.  You asked for comments.  I''m afraid the ones you received in challenge did you a disservice.</td>', 'This would look better if something in it were sharp, preferably the vegetables.  Lowering your aperture would allow you to increase your shutter speed and freeze the motion.  This would certainly sharpen things up. Losing the yellow tint in the air bubbles on the left side would also help.  The picture would have much more impact with just the color of the vegetables, the white of the water, and the black background. Really the big issue here is not freezing the motion. Hope that helps.  You asked for comments.  I''m afraid the ones you received in challenge did you a disservice.', '2007-02-19 11:47:03.000000', NULL, 0),
