(3382309, 467340, 27482, '<td valign="top">Haha, well gotta agree with the border, sorry but it´s absolutely dreadful :)<br/> <br/>You asked about the lighting and I actually think it´s pretty good.  Maybe if you want more natural lighting is to use a big north window during the day and a tripod, but this is not bad lighting at all.  I gotta say I don´t care for the backround though, either would have wanted it pitch black orsomething a bit more natural, like the fruit basket on the top of a desk and the backround out of focus.</td>', 'Haha, well gotta agree with the border, sorry but it´s absolutely dreadful :) You asked about the lighting and I actually think it´s pretty good.  Maybe if you want more natural lighting is to use a big north window during the day and a tripod, but this is not bad lighting at all.  I gotta say I don´t care for the backround though, either would have wanted it pitch black orsomething a bit more natural, like the fruit basket on the top of a desk and the backround out of focus.', '2007-02-19 16:44:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3382365, 465839, 66952, '<td valign="top">Well done, even if you were "selling out." I thought of doing the same thing, but didn''t have a clear container to throw the fruit into, and figured there''s be 10 people who did it better (like you and Larus, for example).<br/> <br/>A question. Is the orange really kind of a squashed shape, or is that an optical illusion?</td>', 'Well done, even if you were "selling out." I thought of doing the same thing, but didn''t have a clear container to throw the fruit into, and figured there''s be 10 people who did it better (like you and Larus, for example). A question. Is the orange really kind of a squashed shape, or is that an optical illusion?', '2007-02-19 17:05:33.000000', NULL, 0),
