(3382943, 466908, 11854, '<td valign="top">Sorry, I gave this a 4 in voting. It seemed a bit OOF and the white of the cottage cheese(?) gave it an odd look.</td>', 'Sorry, I gave this a 4 in voting. It seemed a bit OOF and the white of the cottage cheese(?) gave it an odd look.', '2007-02-19 20:08:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3382950, 467442, 73564, '<td valign="top">How awesome is this? Well let me tell ya, Outragously Awesome!!!! Fantastic!!!!</td>', 'How awesome is this? Well let me tell ya, Outragously Awesome!!!! Fantastic!!!!', '2007-02-19 20:10:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3382958, 467111, 11854, '<td valign="top">I adored this shot and gave it a 6, even though I thought it DNMC. I''m usually not the DNMC police, but it is not a fruit or a vegetable. This would definitely make top ten in a fungus challenge though! LOL!</td>', 'I adored this shot and gave it a 6, even though I thought it DNMC. I''m usually not the DNMC police, but it is not a fruit or a vegetable. This would definitely make top ten in a fungus challenge though! LOL!', '2007-02-19 20:11:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3382998, 467075, 66952, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote in this challenge, but I saw in the forums you were looking for critique. I think the main problem is that the motion isn''t stopped. If you look at the "splashing water fruits and vegetables" that scored well, you see that the motion is completely stopped, and the fruits are all absolutely sharp. The only way I''ve found to really stop motion in this kind of shot is to shoot in a dark room and use flash to stop the motion. A flash will fire faster than your fastest shutter speed. You also might want to use a white sheet or something (waterproof) out of the frame on the sides to block any stray colors from showing up. <br/> <br/>The thing that''s both a blessing and a curse with studio shots is that you  have full control over everything in the shot. This kind of control can create an amazing shot, but also forces you to be much more exacting with every aspect of the shot. Good luck in the next challenge.</td>', 'I didn''t vote in this challenge, but I saw in the forums you were looking for critique. I think the main problem is that the motion isn''t stopped. If you look at the "splashing water fruits and vegetables" that scored well, you see that the motion is completely stopped, and the fruits are all absolutely sharp. The only way I''ve found to really stop motion in this kind of shot is to shoot in a dark room and use flash to stop the motion. A flash will fire faster than your fastest shutter speed. You also might want to use a white sheet or something (waterproof) out of the frame on the sides to block any stray colors from showing up.  The thing that''s both a blessing and a curse with studio shots is that you  have full control over everything in the shot. This kind of control can create an amazing shot, but also forces you to be much more exacting with every aspect of the shot. Good luck in the next challenge.', '2007-02-19 20:20:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3383036, 467456, 11854, '<td valign="top">I thought this was cute and gave it a 6 in voting. The colors are vibrant, the sharpness is spot on. I love the tilt to it.</td>', 'I thought this was cute and gave it a 6 in voting. The colors are vibrant, the sharpness is spot on. I love the tilt to it.', '2007-02-19 20:26:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3383043, 467245, 70828, '<td valign="top">Screw all the naysayers. I think this is a BRILLIANT image!</td>', 'Screw all the naysayers. I think this is a BRILLIANT image!', '2007-02-19 20:27:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3383168, 467111, 66384, '<td valign="top">I love this, especially the separation of the mushrooms from the background. They pop out of the picture. I like the colors in the reflection and the texture the screen adds. I gave it a 10 and have no problem with mushrooms in a veggie challenge -- I put them in my veggie omelets.</td>', 'I love this, especially the separation of the mushrooms from the background. They pop out of the picture. I like the colors in the reflection and the texture the screen adds. I gave it a 10 and have no problem with mushrooms in a veggie challenge -- I put them in my veggie omelets.', '2007-02-19 21:00:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3383173, 467442, 45519, '<td valign="top">Very creative with excellent execution, both photographically and artistically!  Congrats on a well deserved blue.</td>', 'Very creative with excellent execution, both photographically and artistically!  Congrats on a well deserved blue.', '2007-02-19 21:04:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3383181, 467183, 66384, '<td valign="top">Interesting processing. They look like bronze.</td>', 'Interesting processing. They look like bronze.', '2007-02-19 21:08:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3383190, 466857, 69246, '<td valign="top">What if, instead of totally desaturating the fruit, you partially desaturated it. Basically, a color gradient from candy to fruit.</td>', 'What if, instead of totally desaturating the fruit, you partially desaturated it. Basically, a color gradient from candy to fruit.', '2007-02-19 21:10:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3383204, 466616, 54674, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by girlwithpistol:</b></div><hr/><i> I think if the colours were burnt a little more and there wasn''t so much noise, this would make an even more amazing photo.  I like the idea and colours used, though.  :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment.  Correcting noise sounds like an easy technical fix but I''m not familiar with details.   Any suggestions what to look for and how to correct?</td>', 'Originally posted by girlwithpistol: I think if the colours were burnt a little more and there wasn''t so much noise, this would make an even more amazing photo.  I like the idea and colours used, though.  :)   Thanks for the comment.  Correcting noise sounds like an easy technical fix but I''m not familiar with details.   Any suggestions what to look for and how to correct?', '2007-02-19 21:13:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3383208, 467254, 66384, '<td valign="top">Such a funny face. I think this is great. You created a very attractive classic still life with a hidden joke in it.</td>', 'Such a funny face. I think this is great. You created a very attractive classic still life with a hidden joke in it.', '2007-02-19 21:14:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3383237, 466765, 66384, '<td valign="top">Jeannie, this is so attractive. Everything looks so fresh and perfect. The colors are excellent and I like the lighting, composition and DOF. I gave it an 8.</td>', 'Jeannie, this is so attractive. Everything looks so fresh and perfect. The colors are excellent and I like the lighting, composition and DOF. I gave it an 8.', '2007-02-19 21:22:57.000000', NULL, 0),
