(3430514, 466935, 42013, '<td valign="top">I''m not an expert on splash shots/heck, i''m not even an amateur ;) but a couple of things strike me.<br/> <br/>One--See if you can light more from the side...possibly by bouncing your flash of of a white posterboard. I may be wrong but it looks like the flash is straight on. More side lighting will give a pleasing dimension to your shadows. Also looks as if it could have been bumped in exposure a bit.<br/> <br/>I do like the series of bubbles radiating around the top of the lime. With just a touch more focus the picture would really pop! I think these shots are harder than they first appear.  mark</td>', 'I''m not an expert on splash shots/heck, i''m not even an amateur ;) but a couple of things strike me. One--See if you can light more from the side...possibly by bouncing your flash of of a white posterboard. I may be wrong but it looks like the flash is straight on. More side lighting will give a pleasing dimension to your shadows. Also looks as if it could have been bumped in exposure a bit. I do like the series of bubbles radiating around the top of the lime. With just a touch more focus the picture would really pop! I think these shots are harder than they first appear.  mark', '2007-03-05 12:26:22.000000', NULL, 0),
